
This tar files contains clang and other tools to compile libraries and
binaries in Android

Also included is the Android NDK version r27b and version r27c.

The default NDK is still r27b; to use the NDK r27c either change the variable NDK in the file 

/data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env 

or set the variable NDK to r27c before sourcing the file /data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env :

NDK=r27c source /data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env 


Usage:

unpack the tar file in 

/data/local/tmp

this creates the directories with the tools in the directory 

/data/local/tmp/sysroot


execute the script to configure the clang environment

/data/local/tmp/sysroot/create_clang_env.sh


To init the clang environment source the file

/data/local/tmp/sysroot/bin/init_clang19_env

Note: This must be done once in each adb session using this clang toolchain

The default pkg-config tool configured is pkg-config 0.19; to use pkgconf instead of pkg-config set the environment variable PKG_CONFIG 

PKG_CONFIG=/data/local/tmp/sysroot/usr/clang19/bin/pkgconf

The include file sysroot/usr/include/add_missing_definitions.h contains dummies for functions missing in Android

The dummy library sysroot/usr/lib/libmylib.so can be used to create libraries that are needed in the Makefile of a tool but are not necessary in Android (like libpthreads.so).
Simply create a symbolic link for the missing library to libmylib.so


